# Rust build-artifact dirs, why "target" appears four times below:
# *-target/ is a SUFFIX glob (catches q147-target/) but misses a
# PREFIX-named dir. This org names target dirs at both ends -
# target-codex-backends/ (quire-specification, quire-protocol,
# quire-observation), target-fr151/ (quire-spec-language),
# target-coverage and target-msrv (quire-analyze) all exist today and
# survive only on hand-written anchored lines naming each one. target-*/
# closes that gap so a future target-q999/ doesn't sail past this
# pattern the way q147-target/ sailed past the old anchored /target.
target/
*-target/
target-*/
.worktrees/
Cargo.lock.bak
*.swp
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
